      <user_rating>5</user_rating>
      <!-- MEASURED 2026-08-31 on a real feed: Goodreads writes a single-digit day
           with NO leading zero ('Sat, 1 Aug 2026 ...'); four of its 49 items were
           this shape. strptime's %d accepts an unpadded day too, so this item pins
           the feed's real shape, not a parser choice. It is also the record's
           WINNING item: added 2026-07-13 (feed position 2, third-most-recent add),
           read 2026-08-01 (the most recent read date in this fixture), so the
           re-sort has to both parse this date AND rank it above two items that were
           added more recently but read longer ago. -->
